Radio page spacing follows the theme

The radio page set its own spacing in pixels, tuned against Footstrap. Under Vantage three
things came out wrong:

- The Neighbour cells card touched the Serving cells card above it. The cards in the
  overview grid drop their section margin so the grid gap spaces them, and nothing spaced
  the grid itself from the card that follows it.
- "Auto refresh" and "Auto scan" broke onto two lines. Vantage gives every select
  width: 100%, so the select took the whole label and squeezed its text.
- Buttons and selects were 38px against Vantage's 36px controls (44px on touch), and the
  gaps between cards were 12px against the 16px of every other Vantage page.

The page column now spaces its blocks with one flex gap and clears each block's own margin,
so the rhythm cannot depend on which theme margin applies where. The gap, radii and control
height read Vantage's exported --v-* tokens first, Footstrap's --fs-* radii next, and keep
the old literals for any other theme, so Footstrap and Bootstrap look as before apart from
the restored space above Neighbour cells. The select keeps its own width.

Applies to: the 3ginfo feed pin, after 0004 and 0005.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT, like 0004.

